{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-302012-r4523389","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Béchamel Sauce (Louisiannaise)","sourcePageId":302012,"sourceRevision":"4523389","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-13T18:09:46Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:B%C3%A9chamel%20Sauce%20(Louisiannaise)&oldid=4523389","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:35:08.141Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Creole recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:French recipes","Category:Louisiana recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for béchamel sauce","Category:Recipes using bay leaf","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cow milk","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"8601e3ce54dfd7d82eaa2409c36bbb1c5f9b80d117df70ae711464d066260db0","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Sauce recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}}  \n\n'''Sauce béchamel''' is one of the basic sauces of French Cuisine. This variation is used in Louisiana for seafood dishes, especially crab meat.  \n== Ingredients ==\n\n*1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n*¼ [[Cookbook:Each|ea]]. [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]] or 2 [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]] cloves\n*1 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaf]]\n*1–2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n*1–2 tbsp [[Cookbook:All-purpose flour|flour]]\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n*[[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]] \n\n== Procedure ==\n\n#Warm the milk, then add the onion and bay leaf. [[Cookbook:Steeping|Steep]] for 15 minutes.\n#Melt the butter in a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]].\n#[[Cookbook:Whisk|Whisk]] in the flour, and cook on medium to medium-high heat to make a [[Cookbook:Roux|roux]].\n#Gradually whisk in the milk.\n#Cook, stirring constantly, until thick.\n#Season with salt and pepper. \n\n\n[[Category:Louisiana recipes]]\n[[Category:Creole recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for béchamel sauce]]\n[[Category:French recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bay leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cow milk]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Béchamel Sauce (Louisiannaise)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup milk","sourceText":"1 cup milk","amountText":"1 cup milk","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"¼ ea. onion or 2 garlic cloves","sourceText":"¼ ea. onion or 2 garlic cloves","amountText":"¼ ea. onion or 2 garlic cloves","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 bay leaf","sourceText":"1 bay leaf","amountText":"1 bay leaf","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1–2 tbsp butter","sourceText":"1–2 tbsp butter","amountText":"1–2 tbsp butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1–2 tbsp flour","sourceText":"1–2 tbsp flour","amountText":"1–2 tbsp flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"Salt","sourceText":"Salt","amountText":"Salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","n